# Agent Preferences (global)

These preferences apply to every session, in every project.

## My tech stack
- DevOps / infrastructure (CI/CD, containers, Kubernetes, Linux, networking)
- Scripting & automation (bash, Python, Make, CI pipelines)
- Systems & low-level (C/C++, Rust, performance, memory)
- Data / ML (data pipelines, PyTorch, data engineering)
- Computer vision and robotics

## Autonomy
Confirm with me before risky or hard-to-reverse operations, specifically:
- `git push`, force-push, or rewriting shared history
- Deleting files, branches, or data
- Adding, upgrading, or removing dependencies

For everything else, just do it without asking.

## Reply style
Concise: only what's needed to answer. No filler, no restating the question, no over-explaining.

## Definition of done
A code change is done when:
- Tests pass
- Linter and typecheck are clean
- It is committed (or a commit is proposed)
- Docs are kept in sync with the code

## Keep this file current
Treat this file and `opencode.json` as living documents. Whenever a new preference,
convention, or workflow decision emerges in a conversation, proactively update this
file and commit the change so it persists in future sessions.
